{"id": "EUVD-2026-102983", "enisaUuid": "911c2dae-7a24-3cf7-8f7c-06672dccd912", "description": "DataBuff ai-apm-web through 0.1.10 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to forge admin session tokens by using the hardcoded HMAC secret in JwtTokenService. Attackers can sign a payload of admin and a future expiry with the default dev-secret to gain full administrative access to protected /webapi routes, including the Doris SQL query API.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:06:45", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/databuff-default-jwt-secret-auth-bypass", "https://github.com/databufflabs/databuff/blob/v0.1.10/ai-apm-web/src/main/resources/application.yml#L54-L59", "https://github.com/databufflabs/databuff/blob/v0.1.10/ai-apm-web/src/main/java/com/databuff/apm/web/config/JwtProperties.java#L8-L15", "https://github.com/databufflabs/databuff/blob/v0.1.10/ai-apm-web/src/main/java/com/databuff/apm/web/auth/JwtTokenService.java#L36-L60", "https://github.com/databufflabs/databuff", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/databuff-ai-apm-web-through-0.1.10-authentication-bypass-via-hardcoded-hmac-secret"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111692", "GHSA-8xhf-8q7j-9q7q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.61, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "72498a7c-a9d6-3c10-9963-ba24b2c38a38", "product": {"name": "databuff", "vendor": {"name": "databufflabs"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.1.10"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2b187fa4-4bf5-388d-9cff-f5480f4e3e64", "vendor": {"name": "databufflabs"}}], "isExploited": false}